  "title": "CHAPTER 3: POLITY AND ADMINISTRATION OF KERALA",
  "order": 3,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b6yxx9n",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.1 Constitutional Framework"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Kerala has a unicameral legislative system consisting of the Legislative Assembly and the Governor.",
        "The Chief Minister is the real executive head of the state administration, while the Governor serves as the constitutional head.",
        "The 3-tier Panchayati Raj system in Kerala includes Grama Panchayats, Block Panchayats, and District Panchayats.",
        "The local self-government framework was restructured significantly under the Kerala Panchayati Raj Act of 1994."
      ],
      "id": "fi8gcjx"
    },
